# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Git already normalizes this repository's content to LF, but a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites the working tree to CRLF, which
# breaks two things:
#
#   - gofmt reports every file as unformatted, so `task check` fails on
#     changes that are in fact correctly formatted;
#   - shell scripts, Dockerfiles, and systemd units are copied or embedded into
#     Linux guests, where a CR at the end of each line is part of the command
#     and fails at runtime. The wslc provider's bridge entrypoint is embedded
#     with go:embed and executed by /bin/sh inside the guest, so a CRLF
#     checkout would break it with no local symptom.
#
# eol=lf (rather than plain text=auto) is what overrides core.autocrlf, so this
# holds regardless of a developer's global Git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts: never normalized, never diffed as text. Content detection
# already covers these, but VM and container images are large enough that an
# accidental text conversion would be both silent and destructive.
*.qcow2 binary
*.img    binary
*.raw    binary
*.vhd    binary
*.vhdx   binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.gz     binary
*.zip    binary
*.tar    binary
*.wasm   binary
